WEBVTT

00:18.240 --> 00:29.330
<b>The Reincarnation of
the Strongest Exorcist in Another World</b>

01:32.400 --> 01:36.470
The first match of the second round 
of the Mixed Disciplines Combat Tournament

01:36.470 --> 01:37.660
is about to begin!

01:38.010 --> 01:40.640
First up is Seika Lamprogue!

01:44.830 --> 01:47.080
And his opponent...

01:47.720 --> 01:51.170
is Labinare the puppeteer!

01:51.450 --> 01:56.250
In the first round, his opponent's 
mace got nowhere near him!

01:56.250 --> 01:59.820
But how will he fare against a fellow mage?

02:04.510 --> 02:07.390
Behold my golem!

02:07.390 --> 02:11.810
I've specialized it for anti-magic combat!

02:12.280 --> 02:15.480
So you've got no chance of winning!

02:20.070 --> 02:22.200
Let the battle begin!

02:22.200 --> 02:26.080
Surrender now, while you still can!

02:30.580 --> 02:31.920
Summoning:

02:35.840 --> 02:37.050
Sickle Weasel.

02:40.910 --> 02:44.810
Labinare's golem fell apart!

02:45.120 --> 02:50.560
Seika's powerful wind magic 
tore right through it!

02:50.560 --> 02:53.150
What just happened?

02:53.600 --> 02:56.560
Surrender while you still can, I guess.

03:00.240 --> 03:02.570
I'm sorry! I surrender!

03:09.310 --> 03:10.890
That was close.

03:11.920 --> 03:13.810
How could that have been close?

03:13.810 --> 03:17.500
Summoners aren't allowed in this tournament.

03:17.500 --> 03:20.930
If they caught me using an 
ayakashi, they'd disqualify me.

03:21.410 --> 03:23.730
I see...

03:27.730 --> 03:29.100
Welcome back.

03:29.360 --> 03:30.230
Yifa...

03:31.530 --> 03:34.660
Yeah. Congratulations, Seika.

03:34.660 --> 03:37.230
She was really worried.

03:37.230 --> 03:39.860
After she saw that Kyle guy fight,

03:39.860 --> 03:42.550
she said it would be safer if you just forfeited.

03:42.550 --> 03:45.220
See? I came back in one piece.

03:45.220 --> 03:46.610
I didn't even get hurt.

03:47.240 --> 03:48.330
Yeah...

03:48.330 --> 03:52.390
You sure got that one over with fast, though.

03:52.390 --> 03:55.710
It's always boring, watching you fight.

03:57.620 --> 04:01.610
If you win, are you going 
to join the Royal Guard?

04:01.610 --> 04:03.590
Nope. I'm going to refuse.

04:05.130 --> 04:06.020
I see.

04:06.020 --> 04:07.440
Good.

04:07.440 --> 04:08.380
Why?

04:08.380 --> 04:10.520
N-No reason!

04:10.860 --> 04:13.750
You're talking like I'm sure to win,

04:13.750 --> 04:15.940
but it's not that easy, you know.

04:16.400 --> 04:20.910
For some reason, I just can't picture you losing.

04:20.910 --> 04:22.990
Don't you think so, Yifa?

04:22.990 --> 04:25.950
I don't know. But if he loses...

04:25.950 --> 04:28.890
Yifa, it'll be fine.

04:28.890 --> 04:29.790
Really?

04:30.320 --> 04:31.220
Really.

04:31.820 --> 04:35.460
<i>I'm not lying. This is like 
playing with a puppy for me.</i>

04:35.690 --> 04:37.180
You'd better not!

04:37.180 --> 04:41.560
And now it's time for the next 
match of the second round!

04:41.560 --> 04:47.060
Stop flirting. The new girl's 
fight is about to start.

04:47.060 --> 04:48.140
"Flirting"?

04:48.140 --> 04:50.220
Amyu, we're not...

04:50.990 --> 04:52.170
<i>Mabel...</i>

04:52.170 --> 04:54.690
<i>She made it through the first round easily.</i>

04:55.600 --> 04:57.030
<i>But what about this time?</i>

04:58.230 --> 05:02.280
Howlo is a powerful earth mage of considerable talent!

05:02.280 --> 05:09.200
How will his opponent, Mabel, a new student 
from the Magic Academy, handle a fellow mage?

05:09.710 --> 05:11.740
Let the battle begin!

05:12.790 --> 05:14.320
Rock Blast!

05:20.630 --> 05:21.250
Wha—

05:22.930 --> 05:25.510
Rock Blast! Rock Blast!

05:36.240 --> 05:38.980
Yellow pulses, roars, bursts, and shatters!

05:38.980 --> 05:41.610
Insurmountable, stern, 
unyielding mountains...

05:42.140 --> 05:47.530
<i>Greater magic. He probably realized he 
wasn't getting anywhere with mid-rank magic.</i>

05:53.760 --> 05:56.350
Yellow pulses, roars, bursts and shatters!

05:56.350 --> 05:58.710
Insurmountable, stern, 
unyielding mountains...

06:10.890 --> 06:12.760
What is that?

06:12.760 --> 06:15.310
Probably gravity magic.

06:15.310 --> 06:19.100
She's using it to make her rapiers and throwing 
daggers dozens of times heavier than rock.

06:19.450 --> 06:22.100
But that's pretty tough, isn't it?

06:22.100 --> 06:25.410
If it's heavy, you can't touch it yourself.

06:25.410 --> 06:29.940
So she's triggering the magic right after 
she throws them, or before they hit.

06:29.940 --> 06:32.180
And with no incantation...

06:32.180 --> 06:33.490
Is that even possible?

06:33.900 --> 06:35.690
<i>That caught my eye, too, but...</i>

06:35.690 --> 06:37.600
<i>The way she uses her sword...</i>

06:37.600 --> 06:40.050
<i>That's not something that's easy to learn.</i>

06:40.550 --> 06:42.170
<i>How did she...?</i>

06:59.160 --> 07:00.770
I surrender.

07:00.770 --> 07:03.190
The winner is Mabel Crane.

07:03.630 --> 07:06.320
That was an incredible 
display she just put on!

07:06.320 --> 07:10.610
Looks like nothing can stop the 
sword of the red-haired hero!

07:10.610 --> 07:12.950
<i>Did she say "hero"?</i>

07:13.720 --> 07:16.740
Why do you think she referred to Mabel as a "hero"?

07:16.740 --> 07:18.400
"Why...?"

07:18.910 --> 07:20.580
You didn't know?

07:20.940 --> 07:25.350
The second hero ever to exist was called Mabel.

07:26.530 --> 07:27.990
She uses the same weapon, too.

07:27.990 --> 07:30.010
That's probably why.

07:33.910 --> 07:35.140
<i>I see.</i>

07:35.660 --> 07:37.220
<i>It's all coming together.</i>

07:55.840 --> 07:58.990
I figured you'd be sending your 
messenger pigeons off in the early morning.

08:02.030 --> 08:04.210
You're a demon spy, aren't you?

08:04.860 --> 08:07.040
What are you talking about?

08:07.590 --> 08:09.910
I've got a lot of questions for you.

08:09.910 --> 08:13.160
Like what's in that message 
you gave to the pigeon.

08:13.160 --> 08:15.520
I have to get to work.

08:15.520 --> 08:17.050
Bye, kid.

08:21.400 --> 08:22.430
Phase of wood!

08:22.430 --> 08:24.440
Spell of Binding Vines!

08:26.270 --> 08:27.370
Damn it!

08:27.370 --> 08:29.610
How did you know?

08:30.290 --> 08:33.150
I heard you talking with that informant.

08:34.560 --> 08:37.030
There was no one around, though!

08:38.420 --> 08:41.430
Well, no <i>people</i>, anyway.

08:42.500 --> 08:45.060
I'll admit it was a lot of work
gathering information

08:45.060 --> 08:48.560
from all the shiki
I set up throughout the city.

08:48.560 --> 08:49.550
"Shiki"?

08:50.000 --> 08:53.880
Seika Lamprogue, who are you?

08:55.140 --> 08:59.270
I figured you'd learned the names and 
faces of everybody at the tournament.

08:59.270 --> 09:04.060
Would you tell me what you 
were going to report, too?

09:05.630 --> 09:07.150
I refuse.

09:07.930 --> 09:08.640
Oh.

09:09.440 --> 09:11.360
Are you going to torture me?

09:11.360 --> 09:13.990
I'll never tell you the truth!

09:14.460 --> 09:17.760
I'll ask your soul instead, then.

09:20.070 --> 09:21.210
Summoning:

09:24.200 --> 09:25.260
Satori.

09:26.000 --> 09:29.000
Episode 6: 
Interwoven Plots

09:36.210 --> 09:37.830
What the hell is this...

09:37.830 --> 09:39.660
"...monster?"

09:39.660 --> 09:42.640
"He's a summoner?"

09:42.640 --> 09:43.560
It—

09:43.800 --> 09:45.950
"It talks?"

09:45.950 --> 09:48.880
"It read my mind?"

09:48.880 --> 09:51.180
"No! How?"

09:53.790 --> 09:57.650
<i>Yes. Satori is an ayakashi that reads minds.</i>

09:58.520 --> 10:00.230
So, let's get started.

10:00.230 --> 10:01.990
Who do you report to?

10:02.850 --> 10:04.540
I'm not telling you!

10:07.360 --> 10:09.960
"Bol Bofis, the Slaughter Baron."

10:09.960 --> 10:14.620
"Black... Nobility...  Fortress... Forest"?

10:17.170 --> 10:18.510
And who's his boss?

10:20.220 --> 10:23.510
"I don't... I don't know..."

10:23.510 --> 10:26.880
"Fell Marquis El Edentrad."

10:26.880 --> 10:29.650
"Conjecture... danger... hero..."

10:29.920 --> 10:32.010
There's too much noise.

10:32.010 --> 10:36.430
Let me ask, just to be sure: 
these two are devils, right?

10:36.430 --> 10:38.700
"Yes... yes..."

10:39.020 --> 10:41.780
"Louwyck... Louwyck..."

10:41.780 --> 10:44.490
"Demon territory. East-northeast..."

10:44.490 --> 10:46.870
"Near the imperial border..."

10:46.870 --> 10:51.330
"The commercial resources... 
located outside the city..."

10:51.330 --> 10:55.270
And this is concerning the hero, right?

10:55.270 --> 10:56.460
"Yes."

10:57.020 --> 11:00.120
"How does he know about the birth of the hero?"

11:00.120 --> 11:03.640
"That's it... no... the demon side..."

11:03.640 --> 11:05.120
"From a spy?"

11:05.120 --> 11:08.880
"Only a few know... human..."

11:08.880 --> 11:10.440
"How much does he know?"

11:10.800 --> 11:12.700
Don't worry about me.

11:12.700 --> 11:15.230
Tell me the name of the 
hero you're spying on.

11:15.860 --> 11:18.610
"Mabel Crane."

11:19.920 --> 11:22.160
And why do you think she's the hero?

11:22.160 --> 11:26.830
"The year of her birth matches 
that of the prophecy..."

11:27.310 --> 11:31.090
"She's the right sex, 
and has the right hair color."

11:31.090 --> 11:33.360
"And she's strong..."

11:33.360 --> 11:34.580
"And..."

11:35.520 --> 11:42.220
"Both the spy and assassin we sent 
to the school last year disappeared."

11:42.220 --> 11:45.180
"But... the strangeness in 
the year she enrolled..."

11:45.180 --> 11:47.380
"The possibility of disinformation..."

11:47.380 --> 11:49.290
"And the rumors..."

11:49.770 --> 11:53.230
"'Mabel Crane is the hero.'"

11:53.980 --> 11:57.150
"The informants all speak of her."

11:57.150 --> 11:59.820
All right, that'll do.

12:01.080 --> 12:03.050
Thank you very much.

12:03.050 --> 12:05.370
You told me what I needed to know.

12:09.700 --> 12:12.100
Well done, Satori.

12:13.620 --> 12:15.920
I'll give you your reward: you can eat him.

12:18.840 --> 12:22.280
Wh-What? Eat me?

12:22.280 --> 12:24.970
No! You're kidding, right?

12:24.970 --> 12:27.760
Get away from me! No!

12:30.680 --> 12:32.530
"Don't eat me!"

12:33.640 --> 12:35.130
"It hurts!"

12:35.670 --> 12:36.660
"I'm scared!"

12:45.260 --> 12:46.490
"Poor man."

12:46.840 --> 12:48.480
"I had no choice."

12:48.480 --> 12:51.120
"It was too dangerous to let him live."

12:51.710 --> 12:54.620
Don't read my mind, Satori.

12:55.590 --> 12:56.790
Or I'll kill you where you stand.

13:00.430 --> 13:01.880
Thank you.

13:01.880 --> 13:03.390
You can go back now.

13:12.580 --> 13:15.050
S-Seika...

13:15.830 --> 13:18.360
Sorry. I scared you, didn't I?

13:25.600 --> 13:28.820
Now then, let's see what's in this message...

13:31.130 --> 13:34.950
Crap. I should've asked 
how to decode the message.

13:35.440 --> 13:38.670
At least I know what the school's after now.

13:38.670 --> 13:40.420
What?

13:40.870 --> 13:45.610
Have the false hero, Mabel, 
win and attract attention.

13:47.000 --> 13:51.560
They need to keep the demons 
away from the true hero, Amyu.

13:52.430 --> 13:55.120
What makes you think that?

13:55.120 --> 14:00.310
When Cordell found her, 
the school probably did, too.

14:01.050 --> 14:03.670
So the demons use human spies, then?

14:03.670 --> 14:07.150
The empire uses demon spies, too.

14:07.410 --> 14:13.250
But the demons lost sight of who 
she was immediately afterwards.

14:13.790 --> 14:19.830
Because I killed the spy and assassin 
who were the only ones who knew.

14:19.830 --> 14:21.460
I see.

14:21.850 --> 14:26.170
And you're not curious about 
where that Mabel girl came from?

14:26.170 --> 14:28.300
Well, it's almost certainly a fake name.

14:28.300 --> 14:29.960
So I am a bit curious.

14:29.960 --> 14:32.640
But I'm not going to go looking into her.

14:32.640 --> 14:36.850
If her being here keeps Amyu 
safe, that's fine by me.

14:37.680 --> 14:43.540
Why did the principal ask you to come here?

14:44.110 --> 14:47.900
We'll know before too long.

14:51.950 --> 14:56.370
<i>Kyle, the evil eye user, 
won his second match just as easily.</i>

14:56.880 --> 14:59.280
<i>His opponent was a tough fighter,</i>

14:59.280 --> 15:02.000
<i>but was helpless in the face of the evil eye.</i>

15:02.000 --> 15:04.630
<i>A young knight named Reinas</i>

15:04.630 --> 15:07.900
<i>easily won his first match 
with earth and wind magic,</i>

15:07.900 --> 15:11.760
<i>and his second with fire and water magic.</i>

15:17.000 --> 15:17.800
Hey there.

15:18.720 --> 15:22.800
Seika Lamprogue. You're pretty good.

15:22.800 --> 15:26.180
I look forward to seeing you in the finals.

15:26.180 --> 15:27.820
Don't lose before then.

15:28.190 --> 15:32.520
<i>Mages who can use four elements 
are pretty rare, they said.</i>

15:32.520 --> 15:34.410
<i>He became the talk of the tournament.</i>

15:34.750 --> 15:38.380
<i>And his opponent in the 
third round forfeited.</i>

15:40.880 --> 15:44.830
<i>My opponent in the third 
round was a necromancer.</i>

15:45.270 --> 15:48.380
Phase of earth and water.
Spell of Cement, Gravel, Water, and Sand.

15:48.920 --> 15:51.840
<i>But he was no match for me.</i>

15:52.190 --> 15:57.100
<i>And as for Mabel, she won handily.</i>

15:58.470 --> 15:59.980
Seika Lamprogue.

16:02.670 --> 16:04.500
Hey, congratulations.

16:05.280 --> 16:07.400
We'll be fighting in the semi-finals, right?

16:07.950 --> 16:09.150
Forfeit.

16:09.920 --> 16:11.070
Why?

16:11.520 --> 16:14.840
This tournament isn't what you think it is.

16:14.840 --> 16:19.430
I'm not sure what kind of tournament 
you believe I think it is...

16:19.430 --> 16:20.250
But no.

16:20.680 --> 16:25.340
If you want to get to the finals, 
then beat me fair and square.

16:25.340 --> 16:27.430
I know you're strong.

16:27.430 --> 16:29.920
Stronger than any of the foes I've faced.

16:29.920 --> 16:32.340
So I may not be able to hold back.

16:32.870 --> 16:35.020
I can't lose this battle!

16:35.020 --> 16:37.660
Please. You don't want to die, do you?

16:39.840 --> 16:40.710
I refuse.

16:42.480 --> 16:45.260
If you don't think you 
can beat me, just say so.

16:45.260 --> 16:47.340
Don't be ridiculous! You...

16:47.340 --> 16:51.230
Zagan forfeits, and the winner is Kyle!

16:52.150 --> 16:54.640
They paid for those tickets, after all.

16:54.640 --> 16:58.390
And two fights got cancelled.
Of course they're angry.

16:59.060 --> 17:02.800
I'm not sure why the 
school chose to send you.

17:02.800 --> 17:05.670
But you need to forfeit this.

17:06.580 --> 17:08.660
We've got good news, everyone!

17:08.660 --> 17:14.670
Since both Reinas and Kyle won 
their third match by default,

17:14.670 --> 17:18.620
we'll hold their semi-final bout today.

17:19.340 --> 17:21.930
I didn't think we'd get 
to see their fight today.

17:22.730 --> 17:23.610
Yeah.

17:24.550 --> 17:25.960
Seika...

17:25.960 --> 17:28.330
Another easy win, huh?

17:30.020 --> 17:31.230
There they are!

17:31.230 --> 17:36.740
The magic knight who's master of 
all four elements, Reinas Keyburun.

17:37.170 --> 17:40.240
And his opponent, 
this tournament's biggest killer...

17:40.240 --> 17:43.350
Will we see more blood this battle?

17:43.350 --> 17:45.870
The evil eye swordsman, Kyle!

17:45.870 --> 17:49.460
They're the two that 
everyone's talking about!

17:49.460 --> 17:52.920
What kind of battle do they have in store for us?

17:54.570 --> 17:56.050
Let the battle begin!

17:56.050 --> 17:58.200
Light shines and illuminates!

17:58.200 --> 17:59.900
Elementals of compassion and protection,

17:59.900 --> 18:04.210
grant me a bright light that 
defies the gaze of death!

18:04.210 --> 18:06.140
Add Evil Eye Tolerance!

18:06.390 --> 18:08.270
A buff against the evil eye?

18:08.270 --> 18:10.810
He uses light magic, too?

18:12.180 --> 18:13.450
Well, young man?

18:13.450 --> 18:15.550
Your eye won't work anymore.

18:15.550 --> 18:16.690
Want to surrender?

18:23.910 --> 18:25.260
Fireball!

18:30.880 --> 18:31.880
Fireball!

18:32.450 --> 18:33.880
Fireball!

18:36.430 --> 18:38.170
What are you...?

18:38.170 --> 18:40.600
Wind Lance! Icicle Lance!

18:38.170 --> 18:40.600
Kyle is unstoppable!

18:40.600 --> 18:41.970
Rock Blast!

18:40.600 --> 18:43.000
What's going on here?

18:43.000 --> 18:45.170
<i>I can only think of one possibility.</i>

18:45.170 --> 18:46.390
<i>Gravity magic.</i>

18:47.900 --> 18:49.690
<i>Just like Mabel.</i>

18:49.690 --> 18:50.980
Damn it.

18:50.980 --> 18:53.360
Create Golem!

19:07.130 --> 19:09.440
Dark-element shadow magic.

19:09.440 --> 19:12.690
That Kyle guy can use magic, too.

19:22.680 --> 19:24.930
<i>That's like the incantations I use.</i>

19:24.930 --> 19:27.500
<i>He's stabbing his own shadow 
into his enemy's shadow,</i>

19:27.500 --> 19:29.310
<i>stopping him from moving.</i>

19:34.400 --> 19:36.880
The whistle has been blown!

19:36.880 --> 19:39.780
The judges have declared a winner!

19:40.210 --> 19:42.350
The winner is Kyle!

19:42.350 --> 19:44.450
He will proceed to the finals!

19:58.430 --> 20:00.930
The final battle's tomorrow, huh?

20:01.500 --> 20:02.380
Yup.

20:02.380 --> 20:05.550
Once tomorrow's over, 
we can go back to the academy.

20:05.940 --> 20:08.750
You're really going to 
lose tomorrow, aren't you?

20:08.750 --> 20:11.720
You're not thinking of winning, right?

20:11.720 --> 20:13.410
No way.

20:13.410 --> 20:15.000
You're going to sleep?

20:15.000 --> 20:15.560
Yup.

20:16.070 --> 20:18.220
I will, too, then.

20:22.530 --> 20:24.110
What's gotten into you?

20:24.880 --> 20:27.030
Let's sleep in the same bed again!

20:27.330 --> 20:28.980
We always sleep in the same bed.

20:28.980 --> 20:31.580
I mean me sleeping next to you!

20:31.580 --> 20:35.860
I haven't been able to 
take human form in ages!

20:35.860 --> 20:36.880
Well...

20:46.880 --> 20:48.440
<i>W-We mustn't!</i>

20:48.440 --> 20:52.270
<i>I'm a fox! I can't mate with a human!</i>

20:58.170 --> 21:01.610
That's a rather rude way to 
interrupt a man's sleep, Mabel.

21:13.850 --> 21:14.750
Phase of wood.

21:14.750 --> 21:16.370
Spell of Binding Vines!

21:22.290 --> 21:24.670
Sorry, but you'll have to leave.

21:24.940 --> 21:27.800
Phase of sunlight. Spell of Internal Release.

21:33.840 --> 21:34.940
<i>She's strong.</i>

21:35.570 --> 21:39.680
<i>If she's come to take my life, 
it's dangerous to let her go.</i>

21:39.680 --> 21:40.900
What's going on?

21:41.390 --> 21:43.190
Stop making all that racket!

21:43.840 --> 21:45.780
It's rude to interrupt.

21:54.760 --> 21:57.040
Seika, um...

21:57.040 --> 21:58.380
What was that?

21:58.380 --> 22:01.540
A trial run of tomorrow's battle, I guess.

22:01.540 --> 22:03.970
Okay, I've made my choice, Yuki.

22:04.540 --> 22:06.550
She came all the way to my room to see me.

22:07.140 --> 22:09.270
Let's spend the night with her.
